# Build output from `quarto render`. All regenerable — see AGENTS.md.

# Quarto intermediates
*_cache/
*_files/
.quarto/
book/_book/
*.quarto_ipynb
*.rmarkdown

# Rendered HTML (regenerate with `quarto render`)
*.html

# LaTeX / tikz intermediates. Quarto writes one tikz<hash>.{tex,log,aux,pdf}
# per tikz figure into the repo root on every render. The hash-named files are
# generated; tikz-matrix-macros.tex is hand-written source and is NOT.
tikz*
!tikz-matrix-macros.tex
# The book's tikz sources and their pre-rendered SVGs are hand-maintained
# inputs (see `make tikz`), not build output.
!book/tikz/
!images/tikz-*.svg
latex_output/
*.log
*.aux
*.synctex.gz
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.out
*.toc
*.nav
*.snm
*.vrb

# The local paper archive is committed in full — PDFs included. They are
# immutable once fetched, so git stores each exactly once. See AGENTS.md.

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Editor scratch
*.mw
*~
